=== help
help ? or esc closes ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Run the program
  s space    run to the next step anywhere, including inside this one
  n          run this step whole; stop at the next step at this level or above
  f          run until the loop, parallel, switch, or call around this step is l
  c          run to the next breakpoint, or the end
  b          return to the previous stop (a session that can step back)
  r          return to the nearest earlier breakpoint stop, or the first
  g          go to a point of the timeline, counted from 0, in one move (a sessi
  p          hold at the next step boundary

Move
  up k       move up a row
  down j     move down a row
  enter      open or close the row (click does the same)
  right l    open the row
  left h     close the row, or go to its parent
  PgUp       up a page
  PgDn       down a page
  home       first row
  end G      last row

Screen
  tab        focus the next pane (click a pane to focus it)
  shift+tab  focus the previous pane
  : /        type a command; every verb below works there
  i          inspect the selected scope row in the console
  ?          show or hide this help
  q          detach and let the run go on unattended
  ctrl+c     leave at once and release the run, like quit
  ctrl+d     leave and release the run (an empty console line)

Type in the console
  until <step>  run to that step (an id or an address like pages[2]/page); a con
  break <step> [hit <n>] [if <expr>]  stop there, when the count and condition a
  log <step> <message>  record the message at every arrival without stopping; {e
  catch none|uncaught|all  stop where a step fails
  delete <step>|log <step>  remove that breakpoint, or that logpoint
  clear  remove every breakpoint, whoever set it
  breakpoints  list breakpoints and their hit counts
  inspect <expr>  evaluate a read-only CEL expression at this stop
  expand <expr> [from <n>]  list a map's or list's children
  scope  list what this stop can name
  complete <partial-command>  list what could be written at the end of that text
  status  where the run is, and why
  backtrace  the step and every container around it
  detach  clear breakpoints and let the run go on unattended
  help  this list

